#exception-box(title: "THE SEVEN FATAL CUET TRAPS")[
  1. *Interim PM vs Substantive PM:* Gulzarilal Nanda was twice interim/caretaker PM (1964, 1966); Shastri and Indira were the formally elected substantive Prime Ministers.
  2. *State Assembly Losses in 1967:* Congress failed to win majority in *7 states* at polls, plus *Haryana* lost via post-poll defection, creating *8 non-Congress governments*.
  3. *DMK Standalone Majority:* In Madras (1967), DMK won an *absolute standalone majority* (137/234 seats), NOT a coalition. First regional party to do so.
  4. *Congress (O) vs Congress (R):* Congress (O) = Organisation (Syndicate bosses); Congress (R) = Requisitionists (Indira Gandhi's new party).
  5. *1969 Presidential Duel:* N. Sanjiva Reddy was the official nominee who *lost*; V.V. Giri was the Independent candidate who *won* on second-preference votes.
  6. *Privy Purses Abolition:* Struck down by Supreme Court in *Madhav Rao Scindia (1970)*; abolished permanently by the *26th Amendment Act (1971)*.
  7. *Restored vs Original System:* Indira restored Congress *electoral dominance*, but NOT the inclusive internal-consensus umbrella described by Rajni Kothari.
]

