Fifteen authentic CUET UG examination-standard multiple-choice questions testing conceptual, chronological, institutional, and factual mastery. Marking scheme: $+5$ for correct answer, $-1$ for incorrect attempt.

== Part 1: Successions, 1967 Earthquake & Non-Congressism

#mcq(1, [Who succeeded Jawaharlal Nehru as the Prime Minister of India in June 1964 following a consensus process led by Congress President K. Kamaraj?], (
  [Morarji Desai], [Gulzarilal Nanda], [Lal Bahadur Shastri], [C. Rajagopalachari],
))

#solution(1, [Lal Bahadur Shastri was unanimously chosen as Prime Minister in June 1964 following extensive party consultations conducted by Congress President K. Kamaraj. Gulzarilal Nanda served merely as interim caretaker for a few days.], answer: [C])

#mcq(2, [The historic slogan "Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan" was coined by Prime Minister Lal Bahadur Shastri during which critical phase?], (
  [The 1962 Sino-Indian War], [The 1965 Indo-Pak War and acute agrarian food crisis], [The launch of the Second Five Year Plan], [The 1967 General Elections],
))

#solution(2, [Shastri coined "Jai Jawan, Jai Kisan" during the 1965 war with Pakistan to salute the dual pillars of national defense and food self-sufficiency during severe agrarian distress.], answer: [B])

#mcq(3, [The doctrine of "Non-Congressism", arguing that opposition parties must unite to overthrow Congress dominance because it was undemocratic and pro-rich, was propounded by:], (
  [Dr. Rammanohar Lohia], [Jayaprakash Narayan], [Acharya J.B. Kripalani], [C.N. Annadurai],
))

#solution(3, [Dr. Rammanohar Lohia, the eminent socialist theoretician, formulated the concept of "Non-Congressism" to consolidate the fragmented opposition vote and overthrow the Congress monopoly.], answer: [A])

#mcq(4, [In the 1967 Fourth General Elections, how many state legislative assemblies saw Congress lose power, leading to the creation of SVD coalition ministries?], (
  [Four states], [Six states], [Eight states (7 at polls + Haryana through defection)], [Eleven states],
))

#solution(4, [Congress failed to win an absolute majority in 7 states at the polls (Punjab, Haryana, UP, Bihar, WB, Orissa, Madras, and Kerala previously), and lost Haryana immediately via defection, creating 8 non-Congress state governments.], answer: [C])

#mcq(5, [The notorious political catchphrase "Aaya Ram, Gaya Ram" was coined by Rao Birender Singh after an MLA named Gaya Lal repeatedly defected between parties in which state?], (
  [Punjab], [Haryana], [Uttar Pradesh], [Rajasthan],
))

#solution(5, [Gaya Lal was an MLA from Hassanpur in Haryana who defected three times within a fortnight in 1967, prompting Rao Birender Singh's famous press quip "Gaya Ram is now Aaya Ram".], answer: [B])

