== Part 2: The Great Split of 1969 & Minority Governance

#mcq(6, [In July 1969, Prime Minister Indira Gandhi initiated a dramatic leftward policy shift by promulgating an ordinance that nationalised how many major commercial banks?], (
  [14 major commercial banks], [10 major commercial banks], [20 major commercial banks], [8 major commercial banks],
))

#solution(6, [Indira Gandhi promulgated an executive ordinance on 19 July 1969 nationalising 14 major private commercial banks with deposits exceeding Rs 50 crore, leading to the resignation of Morarji Desai.], answer: [A])

#mcq(7, [In the watershed 1969 Presidential Election, who won as an Independent candidate supported by Indira Gandhi's call for a "conscience vote", defeating official nominee N. Sanjiva Reddy?], (
  [Dr. Zakir Husain], [V.V. Giri], [Fakhruddin Ali Ahmed], [Giani Zail Singh],
))

#solution(7, [Vice-President V.V. Giri contested as an Independent and won on second-preference votes after Indira Gandhi urged MPs and MLAs to cast a "conscience vote" against official nominee Sanjiva Reddy.], answer: [B])

#mcq(8, [Following the formal split of the Indian National Congress in November 1969, what was the official designation given to the faction led by the Syndicate?], (
  [Congress (Requisitionists)], [Congress (Indira)], [Congress (Secular)], [Congress (Organisation)],
))

#solution(8, [The faction led by the Syndicate bosses (S. Nijalingappa, K. Kamaraj, Morarji Desai) was officially designated Congress (Organisation) or Congress (O), while Indira's party was Congress (R).], answer: [D])

#mcq(9, [What was the central pro-poor slogan deployed by Indira Gandhi's Congress (R) in the 1971 Fifth Lok Sabha elections to counter the Grand Alliance's slogan "Indira Hatao"?], (
  [Garibi Hatao (Abolish Poverty)], [Jai Jawan Jai Kisan], [Sampoorn Kranti], [Congress Lao, Desh Bachao],
))

#solution(9, [Indira Gandhi electrified the electorate by countering the opposition's negative "Indira Hatao" with her transformative, pro-poor positive campaign pledge: "Garibi Hatao" (Abolish Poverty).], answer: [A])

#mcq(10, [In the 1971 Fifth General Elections, how many seats did Indira Gandhi's Congress (R) secure on its own in the Lok Sabha?], (
