== Part 3: Institutional Transformation & Core Analysis

#mcq(11, [Which constitutional amendment abolished the Privy Purses and privileges guaranteed to the former rulers of princely states in 1971?], (
  [24th Amendment Act], [26th Amendment Act], [42nd Amendment Act], [44th Amendment Act],
))

#solution(11, [The 26th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1971, abolished Articles 291 and 362 of the Constitution, permanently ending all privy purses and special royal titles granted to former princes.], answer: [B])

#mcq(12, [The Samyukta Vidhayak Dal (SVD) coalition government formed in Uttar Pradesh in 1967 was headed by which prominent agrarian leader who defected from the Congress?], (
  [Chaudhary Charan Singh], [Chaudhary Devi Lal], [Karpoori Thakur], [Chandra Shekhar],
))

#solution(12, [Chaudhary Charan Singh broke away from the Congress party to establish the Bharatiya Kranti Dal (BKD) and headed the landmark SVD coalition ministry in Uttar Pradesh in 1967.], answer: [A])

#mcq(13, [The "Kamaraj Plan", formulated in 1963 to revitalise the Congress organisation, proposed that:], (
  [All opposition parties should merge with the Congress], [The Prime Minister must be directly elected by the public], [The Planning Commission should be dissolved], [Senior cabinet ministers and Chief Ministers should resign government office to dedicate themselves to grassroots party work],
))

#solution(13, [Under the Kamaraj Plan of 1963, senior national ministers and state Chief Ministers resigned their government posts to undertake organizational work, inadvertently elevating Kamaraj as party kingmaker.], answer: [D])

#mcq(14, [Which of the following was NOT a member of the "Syndicate"—the powerful informal group of senior regional leaders within the Congress during the mid-1960s?], (
  [K. Kamaraj], [S.K. Patil], [Jayaprakash Narayan], [Atulya Ghosh],
))

#solution(14, [Jayaprakash Narayan was a socialist leader who had renounced active party politics for the Sarvodaya movement, not a member of the Congress Syndicate (which comprised Kamaraj, Patil, Ghosh, Nijalingappa, etc.).], answer: [C])

#mcq(15, [How did the restored Congress system under Indira Gandhi fundamentally differ from the original "Congress System" conceptualised by political scientist Rajni Kothari?], (
  [It transitioned from a democratic republic to a constitutional monarchy], [It banned all opposition political parties from contesting elections], [It abandoned parliamentary democracy in favor of a presidential system], [It replaced the multi-factional internal consensus umbrella with a highly centralised and personalised command hierarchy reliant on the supreme leader's charismatic mass appeal],
))

#solution(15, [While Rajni Kothari's original Congress System functioned as an inclusive umbrella accommodating diverse internal factions and regional satraps, Indira's restored Congress transformed into a highly centralized, personalized command structure reliant on her direct plebiscitary appeal.], answer: [D])

